2. Calculate the number of digits contributed by the perfect squares of numbers from 32 to 50 (which include triple digit numbers).
3. Calculate the number of digits contributed by the perfect squares of numbers from 51 to 70 (which include triple digit numbers).
4. Calculate the number of digits contributed by the perfect squares of numbers from 71 to 90 (which include triple digit numbers).
5. Calculate the number of digits contributed by the perfect squares of numbers from 91 to the largest two-digit number whose square is less than or equal to 2500 (which include four digit numbers).
6. Sum up all these digits to get the total number of digits in the sequence.

